counterfactuals.output:
1. A diagnostic apparatus for an internal combustion engine, comprising a processor configured to:
receive operational data from a plurality of characteristic sensors associated with the internal combustion engine;
estimate a fuel molecular mixing ratio of a fuel supplied to the internal combustion engine based on the received operational data;
detect a combustion failure within the internal combustion engine based on a comparison of the estimated fuel molecular mixing ratio with a predetermined combustion threshold; and
detect a sensor failure in at least one sensor of the plurality of characteristic sensors based on a discrepancy between the estimated fuel molecular mixing ratio and an expected fuel mixing profile calculated for the internal combustion engine.
